# Test dependencies of the Python package for the CI version matrix
# (Python 3.10-3.13): the wheel is built once per OS by the "Python package"
# job, so maturin is not needed here. Never the vendor package.
#
# One directory per Python version: the versions that resolve differ (numpy,
# pandas and pyarrow drop Python 3.10 and 3.11), and Dependabot recompiles all
# the locks in a directory with the single Python named by the first
# pip-compile header it finds there. Compile on Python 3.12, in this directory:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
# The four requirements.in files are identical apart from this version; change
# them together.
pyarrow>=14
polars>=1.0
pandas>=2.2
